  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $547M in FY2027 to date. The Department of the Treasury recorded 1,608 awards in that period, with an average award size of $340K. Obligations fell 92.2% year over year. The Department of the Treasury's current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date. Historical obligations show a multi-year decline from $10.3B in FY23, $9.3B in FY24, $8.6B in FY25, and $7B in FY26 to $547M in FY27. The top NAICS category in FY2027 to date is Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining at $240M, followed by Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying at $64.3M and Other Computer Related Services at $61.4M. The top vendor in FY2027 to date is STONEX FINANCIAL LTD at $240M, followed by PRIORITY FULFILLMENT SERVICES, INC. at $36.8M and WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC at $36M. These figures show where fiscal activity concentrated in the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What drove the drop in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $547M in FY2027 to date, down 92.2% year over year. Annual obligations were higher in prior years, including $10.3B in FY23 and $9.3B in FY24. The Department of the Treasury's FY2027 total is a fiscal year to date number and is partial. Year-over-year comparisons reflect that partial current-year total against prior full-year totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors received the most in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining received $240M, making it the largest NAICS category in FY2027 to date. Other leading categories include Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying at $64.3M and Other Computer Related Services at $61.4M. STONEX FINANCIAL LTD received $240M, followed by PRIORITY FULFILLMENT SERVICES, INC. at $36.8M and WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC at $36M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of the Treasury spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $547M in FY2027 to date. The Department of the Treasury recorded 1,608 awards and an average award size of $340K, and obligations fell 92.2% year over year. Current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date, and prior full-year obligations included $9.3B in FY22, $10.3B in FY23, $9.3B in FY24, $8.6B in FY25, and $7B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Treasury buy?",
      "a": "The Department of the Treasury bought items and services concentrated in metals and technology. Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining received $240M, Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying received $64.3M, Other Computer Related Services received $61.4M, Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services received $42M, and Paper Mills received $34M. Other categories in the top 10 include Software Publishers, Computer Systems Design Services, Electronic Computer Manufacturing, and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services with values as listed."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Treasury's largest contractors?",
      "a": "The Department of the Treasury's largest contractors in FY2027 to date are STONEX FINANCIAL LTD at $240M, PRIORITY FULFILLMENT SERVICES, INC. at $36.8M, WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC at $36M, CRANE & CO., INC. at $36M, and PMX INDUSTRIES, INC. at $28.2M. Additional top vendors include FCN, INC. at $14.5M, DELOITTE & TOUCHE LLP at $13.9M, ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $8.3M, SICPA SECURINK CORP at $5.9M, and INTERNATIONAL BUSINESS MACHINES CORPORATION at $5.5M."
